    ["和大多数孩子比起来，梅丽莎无疑是特别的。\n她十六岁的时候，已经习惯了清晨五点半起床，步行五十分钟去廷根技术学校。不是为了锻炼，而是这样每周能省下八便士——刚好够一顿有肉的晚餐，或者让班森少加一次班。\n她很少给家里添麻烦。或者说，她已经成熟到能为两个哥哥解决麻烦了。家庭的每一笔开支都经过她的计算，这要归功于她那出色的数学天赋，能把生活安排得井井有条。但这还不够，梅丽莎还要为将来打算——也许只有两个哥哥都过上稳定的生活，她才能停下来。\n她喜欢研究机械。那些捡来的废旧零件，会在她手里奇迹般地变成能跑能跳的小玩意儿。咔哒咔哒的发条声里，每一枚齿轮都精准地履行着自己的职责。秩序感能抚平她心里的焦虑，让她感到前所未有的安心。\n班森和克莱恩总担心她太过懂事，怕她变成一位愁容满面的严肃女士。但梅丽莎也是个可爱的孩子。别人夸她时，她嘴上说“还好”，心里却悄悄开了花。还有第一次吃到克莱恩做的羊肉时——美食对她来说太奢侈了，一个不小心，她就扫光了自己那份。然后红着脸去收拾厨具，生怕被看到那因过分幸福而藏不住的失态。\n她像一枚精准运转的齿轮，把自己嵌进这个家的每个缝隙里。偶尔也会咔哒一声，偷偷快乐一下。"] = "Compared to most children, Melissa is undoubtedly special. \n By the time she was sixteen, she was already used to getting up at 5:30 in the morning and walking for fifty minutes to Tingen Technical School. Not for exercise, but to save eight pence a week—just enough for a dinner with meat, or to let Benson work one less overtime shift. \n She rarely adds trouble to the family. Or rather, she has matured enough to solve problems for her two brothers. Every expenditure of the family is calculated by her, thanks to her excellent mathematical talent, which can arrange life in an orderly manner. But this is not enough, Melissa also has to plan for the future—perhaps only when both brothers have a stable life can she stop. \n She likes to study mechanics. Those discarded parts she picked up would miraculously turn into gadgets that can run and jump in her hands. In the ticking sound of the clockwork, every gear performs its duty precisely. The sense of order can smooth out the anxiety in her heart, making her feel unprecedentedly at ease. \n Benson and Klein are always worried that she is too sensible, afraid that she will become a serious lady with a worried face. But Melissa is also a cute child. When others praise her, she says “it’s okay” on the surface, but her heart is secretly blooming. And the first time she ate the mutton Klein cooked—food is too luxurious for her, and if she wasn’t careful, she would finish her share. Then she would go to clean up the kitchenware with a blushing face, for fear of being seen in a state of being unable to hide her excessive happiness. \n She is like a precisely running gear, embedding herself into every gap in this family. Occasionally, she will click and be secretly happy.",
